    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184-a1">

                <pb facs="0328" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 951.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rick to Capt. Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Butaritari</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: This morning I respectfully asked you
                    to take certain United States official mail and private mail, which I then
                    tendered you. You declined taking it upon certain grounds. I would like to have
                    those grounds in writing. Will you kindly, by the messenger bringing this or
                    otherwise, state in writing your objections and greatly oblige,</p>
                <p>Most respectfully, yours, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Rick.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
